  ("Why are my gutters overflowing?", "Usually a clog, a blocked downspout, gutters that are too small for the roof, or a run without enough slope."),
  ("Why are my gutters sagging?", "Loose or spaced-out hangers, heavy debris, standing water or rotted fascia boards."),
  ("How far should downspouts drain from the house?", "Aim for at least 4 to 6 feet from the foundation."),
  ("Can bad gutters cause a wet basement?", "Yes. Water dumped at the foundation is one of the most common causes."),
  ("How often should gutters be cleaned?", "At least twice a year, more often under trees."),
  ("Are ice dams caused by gutters?", "Ice dams start on the roof when snow melts and refreezes, but clogged gutters make them worse."),
  ("What is fascia board?", "The board along the roof edge that gutters attach to. When it rots, gutters pull away."),
